{{!-- The publication's own recommendations, in whichever Directory layout it picked.

THIS FILE'S NAME IS A CONTRACT, NOT A CHOICE. `{{recommendations}}` renders through
`templates.execute('recommendations', response, …)` (core/frontend/helpers/recommendations.js),
which resolves a theme partial of exactly this name ahead of Ghost's own
`core/frontend/helpers/tpl/recommendations.hbs`. Rename it and the platform's five-item list comes
back.

That is also why the layout picker is read HERE rather than in the template, which is the one
place this theme breaks its own rule that no partial reads `@custom`. The helper owns the render
and takes no arguments through to the partial, and `recommendations` is not a `{{#get}}` resource
(RESOURCES in core/frontend/helpers/get.js lists posts, tags, pages, authors, tiers and
newsletters and nothing else), so there is no way to query the data from a template and dispatch
around it. The `@` frame survives — the helper builds its own with `createFrame(options.data)` —
so `@custom` is readable from in here.

The context is the API response, so the rows are `recommendations` and the guard is on that array.
Ghost's own template guards the same way, and for the same reason every {{#get}} in this theme
does: an empty result is not an error branch. --}}
{{#if recommendations}}
	{{#match @custom.directory_layout "Cover cards"}}
		{{> "directory/rec-cards"}}
	{{else}}
		{{> "directory/rec-rows"}}
	{{/match}}
{{/if}}
